      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it sounds like you're being way too soft on the \"proponents\" side. if the supreme court literally said you can't use \"public safety\" as a reason to bypass the historical standard, then any argument that isn't based on a direct historical analog is, by definition, an invalid legal argument. it's not \"active debate,\" it's just trying to argue against the rule of law. why is it so hard to just say that most modern gun control is now legally indefensible under the current standard?",
